'''IG-101''' was one of the two [[IG-100 MagnaGuard]]s, the other being [[IG-102]],<ref name="CE">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> that served as [[General]] [[Grievous]]'s [[droid]] [[bodyguard]]s aboard the ''[[Invisible Hand]]'' during the [[Battle of Coruscant]]. [[Gender|He]] was programmed to automatically learn combat and refined his combat skills in long training sessions with Grievous. Due to his training, he could wield two [[electrostaff]]s at the same time.<ref name="Altaya">{{EncyclopediaCite|Melee and Ranged Weapons}}</ref>

==History==
[[File:IG-101-SWZ92.png|thumb|left|250px|IG-101 piloting a ''Rogue''-class starfighter on a rocky world]]
At some point prior to the Battle of Coruscant IG-101 piloted a [[Rogue-class Porax-38 starfighter|''Rogue''-class starfighter]] beside a [[Belbullab-22 heavy starfighter]] through a misty ravine on an unidentified rocky world.<ref name="SWZ92">{{FFGXW2|set=Rogue-class Starfighter Expansion Pack|cardname=IG-101}}</ref>

IG-101 was present with [[IG-102]] on the [[Bridge (starship)|bridge]] of the ''Invisible Hand'' as Grievous gloated over the captured [[Jedi]], [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], and [[Anakin Skywalker]]. Skywalker's [[Astromech droid|astromech]], [[R2-D2]], was able to distract those on the bridge for Kenobi to use the force take his [[lightsaber]] back from Grievous, with Skywalker taking his back afterwards. Grievous ordered the droids to attack, with IG-102 focusing Kenobi, and IG-101 focusing on Skywalker. 101 was able to press Skywalker for a while, but the Jedi managed to find an opening in his defense and cut the droid in half at the waist, destroying it.<ref name="Episode III" />

